{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["And Moshe spoke to the heads of the tribes — I was asked in Joniub [name of a city] in the district of Looshron [name of a region in France]: by the plain sense, where do we find any parashah that begins thus? For above it was not said: ״וידבר ה׳ אל משה לאמר: איש כי ידור״ and so on. And how does the parashah begin with Moshe's own words, with no explicit instruction given to him from the mouth of the Almighty? And this is my answer: above it is written: ״אלה תעשו לה' במועדיכם לבד מנדריכם ונדבותיכם״ — that you are required to bring on one of the three pilgrimage festivals because of בל תאחר, as explained in tractate Rosh HaShanah. Moshe went and spoke to the heads of the tribes, who are judges, to instruct Israel the laws of vows, and said to them: the Holy One, blessed be He, commanded me that they should bring their vows and their freewill offerings at the festival, lest they delay their vows. Therefore —" "When a man vows a vow to YHWH — a sacrifice. Or swears an oath — to afflict his soul."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :register {:flags {0 ["the Almighty"]}}, :notes {0 "Place names given in the Hebrew with parenthetical glosses (a city; a region in France); transliterated approximately."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:51:02.759301726Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}